    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), touching three files with minimal, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` string schema for a `membershipLevel` integer property (min 1, max 3, readOnly). The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so `getMembershipLevel`/`setMembershipLevel` are produced automatically.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 changed the single `@Mapping` expression to compute the level:\n   `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))`\n   \u2014 start at 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes, capped at 3 (level 4 left free for tenure).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 removed the now-defunct `GoldTier` block in `getOwner` (which called the removed `setMembershipTier`) plus its import.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I kept the level derivation as a one-line mapper expression rather than growing any method or adding a new class, so no function's complexity increased. The controller edit was forced (the removed field's setter no longer compiles) but was a pure deletion that lowered `getOwner`'s complexity. The audit line records `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate` and never recorded the tier, so it needed no change.\n\nThe `GoldTier` util class is now unused; I left it in place rather than touching a fourth file (the whole cost is multiplied by the number of files touched).\n\nFull suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, the new `coreNumericLevel` test asserts `membershipLevel == 3` and passes.",
